// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
// Provenance: vendored from WebAssembly/wasi-cli, tag v0.2.0 (wit/stdio.wit).
//
// Vendored subset of the canonical WASI Preview 2 cli stderr
// interface.
//
// Source: WebAssembly/wasi-cli, tag v0.2.0
//   https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-cli/blob/v0.2.0/wit/stdio.wit
//
// Trimmed to the get-stderr() reader Capa's experimental --wasi mode
// imports (Stdio.eprintln -> get-stderr ->
// output-stream.blocking-write-and-flush loop). Split out of the
// upstream stdio.wit (which declares stdin / stdout / stderr together)
// into one file per interface so each is independently greppable; see
// stdout.wit for the shared rationale. Same wasi:cli@0.2.0 package as
// environment.wit / stdout.wit; wasm-tools merges the package's .wit
// files when resolving deps/cli/.
//
// Canonical-ABI / unit conventions matching the host wasmtime
// add_wasip2() provides:
//   get-stderr -> output-stream : an OWNED output-stream handle the
//     guest writes the program's standard error to (Stdio.eprintln),
//     captured separately from stdout so the two streams stay distinct
//     (the --wasi host installs a WasiConfig stderr_custom callback;
//     see capa.runtime._wasm_component_host).
//
// The ``package wasi:cli@0.2.0;`` declaration lives ONLY in
// environment.wit (the first cli file): wasm-tools merges every .wit
// file in deps/cli/ into one package and rejects doc comments attached
// to more than one ``package`` item, so this file omits the package
// line and contributes only its interface to the shared package.

interface stderr {
  use wasi:io/streams@0.2.0.{output-stream};

  get-stderr: func() -> output-stream;
}
